cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite this release and the accompanying article."
title: "Graceful or Catastrophic? Sensor-Fusion Resilience of Autonomous-Vehicle Localisation under Coordinated Global Navigation Satellite System Spoofing and Perception Attacks: code and results"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Obafemi
    given-names: Akinwole
    affiliation: "Edinburgh Napier University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6875-1900"
abstract: >-
  Code and result files for a study of multi-sensor localisation fusion under simultaneous GNSS
  spoofing and perception attacks, submitted to IET Radar, Sonar & Navigation. Part A benchmarks
  receiver-level spoofing detectors on the TEXBAT processed observables; Parts B and C replay nuScenes
  v1.0-mini trajectories through a synthetic sensor suite and an extended Kalman filter under GNSS,
  perception and coordinated attacks, comparing five fusion configurations and seven attack detectors.
keywords:
  - GNSS spoofing
  - sensor fusion
  - autonomous vehicles
  - LiDAR odometry
  - perception attacks
  - anomaly detection
